# ms-graph-demo: FastEndpoints API protected by Entra ID, calls Microsoft Graph on-behalf-of the caller.
# No launchSettings: the VS Code launch config sets ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://localhost:5100.
# (A plain `dotnet run` without ASPNETCORE_URLS falls back to Kestrel's default http://localhost:5000.)
@host = http://localhost:5100

# Entra ID access token for THIS API (audience api://<client-id>), acquired outside this file,
# for example: az account get-access-token --scope api://<client-id>/access_as_user --query accessToken -o tsv
#   - GET /me    needs the delegated scope access_as_user
#   - GET /users needs access_as_user, or the app role Users.List (daemon / client credentials)
@token =

### Current user's Graph profile (delegated access_as_user)
GET {{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Directory users, top 25 (access_as_user or app role Users.List)
GET {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Without a token (expect 401)
GET {{host}}/me

### OpenAPI document
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

### Scalar API reference (Development only)
GET {{host}}/scalar/v1
